+/* ---- converted-vertex cache ------------------------------------------------
+ * Most draws feed the same guest vertices every frame (map geometry, props), and
+ * converting them -- index parsing, collapsing repeats, big-endian decode into
+ * float4 slots -- was ~40 % of the FIFO thread with the camera pulled out. A draw
+ * is keyed by everything that decides its reference list and decode (vertex
+ * layout, every used attribute's descriptor and default, base index/offset, the
+ * batches and the raw index bytes); a hit is accepted only when a hash of every
+ * guest vertex byte the draw reads also matches, so a changed buffer is a miss.
+ * A hit draws straight from the stored conversion. RSX_VCACHE=0 turns it off;
+ * RSX_VCACHE_VERIFY=1 converts every hit again and compares (log: [vcache]). */
+
